    logP = 2.1);
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Tromantadine is an antiviral drug used to treat skin infections caused by herpes simplex virus. It is applied topically as a cream and is used in a limited number of countries, mainly in Europe, but is not authorised across the whole European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4463719\">Wikidata Q4463719</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>tromantadine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D06BB02, J05AC03</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13288\">DB13288</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/64377\">64377</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:135163\">135163</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4463719\">Q4463719</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C16H28N2O2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>280.412 g/mol (PubChem CID 64377)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>2.1 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
